7. EPISODE EXPERIENCE

Episodes must be first-class entities.

Users should be able to:

- see episode number
- title
- release date
- runtime when available
- synopsis
- watch status
- mark as watched
- discuss the episode
- see posts associated with that episode

An episode discussion must support spoiler protection.

Example:

Episode 8 Discussion

"Did anyone else notice..."

The UI should understand that this is an Episode 8 conversation and protect users who have not reached Episode 8.

---

8. SPOILER SYSTEM

Spoilers are a fundamental Hallyu problem.

Do not implement spoilers as a simple visual blur only.

Design a contextual spoiler system.

Possible spoiler levels:

- No spoiler
- Episode spoiler
- Season spoiler
- Ending spoiler

A post should be capable of being associated with:

- drama
- season
- episode

The UI should communicate exactly what the user is about to reveal.

Example:

Episode 10 spoiler

Reveal spoiler

After revealing, the user can read the content normally.

---

9. ACTOR EXPERIENCE

Actor pages are an important discovery bridge.

Each actor page should include:

- profile image
- name
- Korean name where available
- biography
- known-for dramas
- filmography
- related actors
- community posts
- trending content
- follow action

Do not build a full IMDb clone.

The purpose is discovery and fandom.

Example:

User discovers an actor from a post → opens actor → discovers another drama → opens drama → joins its community.

